  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The group feature in vrchat is amazing.\n\nIt allows Community moderation and the ability to gather in a location with a shared interest based on the community.  However it's not easy to find good groups unless you go out hunting for one by World hopping and looking at everybody's groups on their profile.\n\nSo what if we had the ability to filter groups based on their player activity and instance creations among other things.\n\nSo it's easier to find groups with an active player base rather than just a random Banner since many groups are just a banner and they have no Community activity.\n\nLike if I could go on the website right now and look up a undertale community that have made at least three instances that have reached a certain amount of players over the past week.\n\nFor example this could be either a filtering system or it could simply be an activity log that could be viewed by everybody",
